    Received string:    "Privacy Policy·
    Effective date: October 27, 2026 · Last updated: October 27, 2026·
    English
    Français
    Español·
    Daymark is a weather app for a limited web/PWA demo and a fuller Android app. Most processing happens in your browser or installed app, but Daymark sends weather, air-quality, and place-search requests directly to Open-Meteo, and the website host processes ordinary request metadata. This policy explains those flows and the choices available to you.·
    Who operates Daymark·
    Daymark is operated by Sami. For questions about this policy or your information, contact skylinelabdev@gmail.com.·
    V2 and V1 transition·
    This policy describes Daymark V2 (version 2.0.0) on the web/PWA and Android. Daymark 1.0.0 may remain installed on a device, or available through Google Play, until V2 reaches its full production release. When V2 is fully released, V1 will be removed from Google Play and official support for V1 will end. Existing V1 installations will not be deliberately disabled.·
    V1 behaved differently: its Android build requested precise location as well as approximate location, used browser/WebView speech recognition for voice input, and could use the device’s default Android text-to-speech voice for French and Spanish narration. Those V1 behaviours apply only while a V1 installation is in use.·
    Weather and place-search requests·
    When the app opens, Daymark loads a forecast for London, its default place. That request is sent directly from your browser or installed app to Open-Meteo and does not require location permission.·
    Weather, air-quality, and place-search data come fromOpen-Meteo. Requests go directly to:·
    api.open-meteo.com — forecasts
    air-quality-api.open-meteo.com — air quality
    geocoding-api.open-meteo.com — place search·
    When you type in the search box, the text you enter is sent to Open-Meteo’s geocoding service to suggest matching places. Daymark does not save your searches. Daymark does not operate a backend or application server for accounts, weather history, searches, or voice data.·
    Location data·
    Daymark does not request location on load. Your device location is used only when you press “Use my location” and grant permission. You can skip location entirely and use the default place or search for a place.·
    The Android app declares ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION only and does not declareACCESS_FINE_LOCATION. Both Android and the web/PWA snap the device-derived coordinates to a 0.025-degree grid with a 0.025-degree minimum step on your device before they are sent to Open-Meteo. At high latitudes, the longitude spacing widens just enough to keep the represented area at least 3 km²; the latitude step never goes below 0.025°. Near London this is roughly 2.8 km north/south and 1.7 km east/west (about 4.8 km²); at high latitude the longitude spacing may be wider. The grid reduces precision but does not anonymise the request: the rounded coordinates still leave your device and are sent to Open-Meteo. The app returns to its default London location when you reload or reopen it.·
    For device location, Daymark also resolves a nearby locality name (for example, a town name) locally from a static GeoNames dataset. The web/PWA downloads the dataset from Daymark’s site and caches it locally; the Android app includes it in bundled assets. No reverse-geocoding service, including GeoNames, receives your coordinates.·
    Web/PWA demo·
    The web/PWA build is a limited weather demo. It has no Ask Daymark microphone control and no “Hear today” narration control. It does not request microphone permission and does not invoke browser speech-recognition or speech-synthesis APIs. The Android app provides the full voice feature set described below.·
    Android voice input (Ask Daymark)·
    Ask Daymark is optional on Android. It starts only when you press the microphone button and grant microphone permission. Recognition uses the bundled Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 int8 model through the sherpa-onnx runtime on the device. Audio is captured temporarily during that user-initiated session and held in memory for recognition; Daymark does not intentionally record or persist the audio or the resulting transcript, and does not send either to a Daymark speech server. The Android voice path has no Android SpeechRecognizer, browser-speech, or online-recogniser fallback in the code. This is a source-level and automated-test statement, not an independently verified packet-level zero-egress claim.·
    Android narration·
    English narration is generated on your device by the bundled Kokoro model. Daymark does not store narration text. French and Spanish narration is not available in V2 and is planned for V2.2; Daymark shows an unavailable message and does not fall back to Android system TTS, a network voice, or browser speech synthesis.·
    Information stored on your device·
    Daymark stores the language code in local storage under daymark.locale. The Android app also stores one private app-state value in SharedPreferences nameddaymark.permissions: the boolean microphone-requested, used only to avoid repeatedly prompting for microphone permission after it has already been requested or denied. Neither value is location, search, transcript, or weather history, and Daymark stores none of those histories. The web/PWA service worker caches app-shell resources, and the locality lookup uses Cache Storage for the static dataset; those are application resources, not user history. The Android app loads the locality dataset from bundled assets.·
    Daymark’s app code does not use cookies, browser session storage, or IndexedDB for user state. You can clear the locale preference and application caches by clearing this site’s or app’s storage in your browser or device settings. Clearing local storage does not automatically delete data already retained by third-party providers such as Open-Meteo.·
    Third parties and retention
    Open-Meteo — weather, air quality, and place search. Its current published privacy notice says it acts as an independent data controller, may keep troubleshooting webserver logs containing sensitive information such as geographical coordinates, and deletes those log files after 90 days. Open-Meteo also receives ordinary network request metadata, including the source IP address and requested URL, to serve the request. Daymark does not use the IP address to identify you or to determine your location; Open-Meteo’s notice says it may process IP addresses for technical reasons. Daymark does not control that retention. Please check Open-Meteo’s currentTerms & Privacy.
    Cloudflare Pages — static hosting for the web/PWA. Cloudflare processes standard website request metadata such as IP address, requested URL, and user agent for delivery, security, and abuse prevention under its ownprivacy policy. Daymark does not claim a fixed Cloudflare retention period.
    GeoNames — the static locality dataset and local nearest-locality lookup. No coordinates are sent to GeoNames.
    The Parakeet speech model, Kokoro narration model, and sherpa-onnx runtime are bundled with the Android app or delivered as app assets. They run on the device for the features described above.·
    Daymark does not include analytics, advertising, tracking pixels, or tracking SDKs. Daymark does not claim that every third-party service is independently secure or that all external processing is retained for zero days.·
    Security·
    The hosted web/PWA is served over HTTPS and uses the site’s configured Content Security Policy. The installed Android app loads bundled local assets; the hosted site’s HTTP security headers do not apply inside its WebView. Daymark is a static bundle with no secrets and no Daymark-operated backend. These are limited, verifiable properties; they are not a guarantee about third-party services or the entire device.·
    Age suitability·
    Daymark is intended for adults aged 18 and over and is not directed to children. This is a Google Play target-audience declaration, not a technical access restriction or an age gate; Daymark does not claim that no minor can access the app. It has no user accounts and Daymark does not maintain profiles, location histories, search histories, or voice-transcript histories. Daymark does not use advertising or tracking IDs. The app does not ask for a date of birth. Selecting an adult audience does not by itself resolve any separate legal or regulatory assessment, including the UK Children’s Code where applicable.·
    Your choices
    Use the default London forecast or place search without granting device location.
    Deny or revoke location permission in your browser or device settings.
    On Android, avoid Ask Daymark and use the weather features without microphone access.
    Deny or revoke microphone permission at any time.
    Clear the locale preference and application caches in your browser or device settings.
    Changes and contact·
    If Daymark’s practices change, this page will be updated and the effective date revised. Questions or concerns: skylinelabdev@gmail.com. Daymark is operated by Sami."

